  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "[SOLVED] I had purchased and was using an asset from the unity store that had shaders made in amplify, and was using cubemaps. swapping these materials to standard fixed the issue. \n\nSince the move to 2019, I've experienced a new issue in my new world Terrarium where seemingly randomly, steamvr will freeze and lockup. Everyone who has experienced this crash describes it as 2 frames freezing and repeating, steamVR locking up, yet you can still hear and communicate with others in the world.\nCollecting logs and checking my own, it seems to crash around after an avatar initializes, however we can't properly replicate it. \nI've removed nearly all Udon scripts from the scene, and re-imported every udon asset including the SDK to the scene with no improvement. I've swapped the video player, and have reduced the world down to just its materials, mesh, and the video player. \nI've been told this has happened elsewhere, but it seems to happen pretty consistently within Terrarium\n\nThis project was made in 2019 2.48f1. it is uploaded on 2019 4.29f1. I have followed the upgrade steps from 2018 just to be safe when versioning up the project. this issue has been since I've created the world..\n\nWe haven't tested it without the video player, but to be happening with two different players makes me think its not the videplayer.\n\nThis problem seems to happen easiest when your in fullbody tracking. the crash has happened on desktop, but its much harder to replicate.\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_26e8e293-08aa-4f72-b5ef-9c54c5f50cc3",
